# THE RHO IMAGE'S CONTEXT (install/docker/Dockerfile builds from the repo
# root so the packaged gem trees and the installer arrive as `--from-checkout`
# reads them): only those are sent; everything else in the monorepo —
# nexus and its node_modules, .git, tmp, coverage — stays out. The evals
# leg (e2e/evals/docker/Dockerfile) builds from the same root. `nexus/`
# has its own Dockerfile with `nexus/` as its context, which this file
# never sees.
*
!sdks/ruby
!agents/rho/rho-runner
!agents/rho/rho-browser
!agents/rho/rho-mcp
!agents/rho/rho-web-tools
!agents/rho/rho-webui
!agents/rho/rho-ingress-telegram
!agents/rho/rho-acp
!agents/rho/rho-acp-client
!agents/rho/rho
!install
!cmctl
# The evals leg's one extra file: the harbor cell's launcher (ACP design
# r2 §5.3), COPYed into the derived image's libexec.
!e2e/evals/docker/rho-acp-launch
# Local dependencies, package output, caches and reports stay out even
# when their parent source tree is included above.
**/.git
**/tmp
**/coverage
**/log
**/node_modules
**/vendor/bundle
**/vendor/cache
**/.bundle
**/pkg
**/*.gem
**/.yardoc
**/_yardoc
**/doc
**/spec/reports
**/test-results
**/playwright-report
**/blob-report
**/playwright/.cache
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]
install/test
install/stack/test
install/stack/test.sh
install/stack/wizard_test.py
install/stack/data
install/stack/.env
install/stack/secrets.env
install/stack/*.env.new
